@{ ViewBag.Title="Help and coordination"; }
<main><section class="pgh-page-banner"><div class="pgh-wrap"><p class="pgh-eyebrow">HGRAS support</p><h1>Connect with the right team.</h1><p>Your hospital's responsible officer is your first contact for resource coordination.</p></div></section><div class="pgh-wrap pgh-page-grid"><section class="pgh-content"><h2>For a resource request or transfer</h2><p>Open your hospital network and use the facility directory to find the responsible officer. Include your transfer number, resource name, quantity and current stage when reporting a delay or discrepancy.</p><a class="pgh-button" href="@Url.Action("Index","Network",new{tab="facilities"})">Find your facility →</a><h2>For account access</h2><p>Your group administrator assigns network membership, your hospital and your operational role. Contact them if you cannot see your hospital workspace.</p><a class="pgh-text-link" href="@Url.Action("HelpCenter")">Read the portal guide →</a></section><aside class="pgh-info-card"><img class="pgh-info-image" src="@Url.Content("~/Content/img/hgras/hospital-exterior.jpg")" alt="Hospital exterior"/><h2>Every handover matters.</h2><p>Confirm quantities, transport arrangements and storage requirements before recording a transfer action.</p></aside></div></main>
